# Changelog
All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]
### Added (BFF M2M client)
- `server/proxy/m2m-client.js`: the BFF now gets its service token from Directory's Backbone managed client (`POST /api/v1/managed-clients/token`, client credentials), the same way `directory-backend` does, instead of the Keycloak password grant. Token cached in Redis (memory fallback) until one minute before it expires, with a distributed lock and shared in-flight requests; secret and token are never logged.
- `getOAuthClient` returns the M2M client when `M2M_CLIENT_ID`, `M2M_CLIENT_SECRET` and `M2M_TOKEN_URL` are set (`M2M_SCOPES` optional); otherwise the legacy Keycloak client is used, so the change is opt-in and reversible by configuration. Controllers are unchanged.
- Tests: `test/m2m-client.test.js` (17 tests, `pnpm test:bff`). Guides: `docs/guides/bff-m2m-client-user-guide.md` and `bff-m2m-client-technical-guide.md`.

### Changed (Angular 22 upgrade)
- Upgraded to **Angular 22** (`^22.2.3`, the same version as `zerobound-frontend`), **NgRx 22**, `zone.js ~0.16.3` and **TypeScript ~6.0.3**, one major at a time with `ng update` (20 -> 21 -> 22) and its automatic migrations. Tailwind CSS is unchanged: `zerobound-frontend` does not use it, so there is no version to align with.
- `tsconfig.json`: removed `baseUrl` (deprecated in TypeScript 6) and prefixed every `paths` target with `./`.
- `auth.guard.spec.ts`: `CanMatchFn` receives a third argument (`currentSnapshot`) in Angular 22; the spec passes it.
- Added `pnpm-workspace.yaml` with `allowBuilds` (pnpm 12 blocks install scripts otherwise) and removed the ignored `pnpm.onlyBuiltDependencies`.
- `Dockerfile`: Node 24 (Angular 22 needs Node 22.22.3+ or 24.15+) and `pnpm-workspace.yaml` copied into the install stages. Not built here.
- Docs: `CLAUDE.md` and `ai/` mention the new versions; guides `docs/guides/angular-22-upgrade-user-guide.md` and `angular-22-upgrade-technical-guide.md`.
- Verified: `ng build` (development and production), `ng run directory-frontend:server:production` and the full suite (530 of 530, same as before). Whole-project function coverage: 49.71 % (Istanbul), unchanged and below the 85 % target.
- Known, not new: the production build warns that `partner-settings.css` exceeds its budget; prerendering logs `NG0955` for the duplicate mock key `mock-logo-5`.

### Fixed (build:ssr)
- `pnpm run build:ssr` failed with `NG8002: Can't bind to 'alt' since it isn't a known property of :svg:svg` in `offer-slider.html`: an `<svg>` has no `alt`, so the translated text (`offer_slider.bookmark_alt`) is now the `title` of the bookmark button container (the icon stays `aria-hidden`).
- Behind it, prerendering `/partner/settings` failed with `NG0200` (circular dependency `HTTP_INTERCEPTORS` / `NotificationService`): since the i18n change `NotificationService` injected `TranslateService` in its field, and `TranslateService` -> `TranslateHttpLoader` -> `HttpClient` -> interceptors -> `ErrorInterceptor` -> `NotificationService` closed a loop. `TranslateService` is now resolved on first use of a message with a key. A new spec fails without the fix.
- Verified: `ng build` (20 prerendered routes), `ng run directory-frontend:server` and the full suite (530 tests). Whole-project function coverage: 49.71% (Istanbul).

### Translations (es / en / fr)
- **All user-facing text is now translated.** 395 keys in `es`, `en` and `fr` (they were 95 / 72 / 0, with `fr.json` empty and invalid). About 300 literal texts of 26 templates, 9 inline templates, 30 notification messages and 13 form-validation messages moved to translation keys; Spanish stays the default language. Texts with parameters use `{{name}}` interpolation (copyright, greetings, counters, phone validation, ...).
- **Parity guard:** `src/app/i18n/i18n-parity.spec.ts` (Karma) fails when a language misses a key, has an empty text or different `{{parameters}}`; `pnpm run i18n:check` also fails when the code uses a key that is not defined. `pnpm run i18n:inventory` lists the literal texts still untranslated (today: none) and `pnpm run i18n:review` writes the review sheet.
- `NotificationService` accepts `{key, params}` besides a plain string (a backend message is still shown as it is) and translates it in the current language; a missing key is shown as the key, so it is visible.
- Fixed on the way: `menu_header.search.aria_label|submit|clear` were used by `app-search` but defined in no language; `en.json` had stale keys (`signing_button`, `menu.business`, `menu.saved`) and a junk empty key (`""`) that were removed; two support-menu tooltips said "Comunícate con nosotros" for Blog and About.
- Development-only panels ("Estado del Formulario (Desarrollo)") are excluded on purpose with `<!-- i18n-ignore:start/end -->`; the developer showcase and usage examples are out of scope.
- **English and French were written by an AI assistant and still need a human review**: `docs/guides/i18n-review.md` lists every text side by side with a checkbox. Language switching in the UI is not part of this change (the default stays `es`).
- Tests: parity spec, `NotificationService` message resolution, `TranslateModule` added to the specs of the translated components. Full suite: 529 tests.
- Code quality (SonarCloud quality gate of PR #91): the i18n scripts sort with an explicit comparator (`byText`, `localeCompare` with a fixed `en` locale; the generated sheets are unchanged), drop an unused import and redundant regex character classes and use `replaceAll`; the double `@ngx-translate/core` imports were merged; two HTTP client specs (`BusinessStatsClient`, `LocationClient`) now assert the encoded URL explicitly. The offer slider markup is valid again (each `<li>` is a direct child of its `<ul>`; the card is the `<div>` inside it, same look and click behaviour), and the card can be focused with Tab and opened with Enter.
- Stacked on the statistics branch (`feature/business-stats-panel`, PR #90) and, through it, on #89: merge #89 and #90 first.

### Business statistics (views)
- Added the **statistics panel** of the partner settings (`/partner/settings/stats`, with a new card in the settings page): total views of a window (last 7, 30 or 90 days), views today, views in the last 7 days and a bar chart with one bar per day (zero days included). Owner only; the backend answers 403 otherwise.
- The public partner page counts one view of a business through `POST .../businesses/{id}/views`. **Only businesses whose id is a UUID are counted and only in the browser** (SSR renders do not count): `PartnerProfileService` still serves mock profiles with numeric ids, so no view is counted from the public page until it reads real businesses.
- No personal data is sent or shown: the request has an empty body, the backend stores only a number per day, and the owner's own visits are not counted.
- Added `BusinessStatsClient` (unwraps the BFF envelope), the NgRx store `businessStats`, `business-stats.model.ts`, `isUuid` helper and `DFC.RelativePath.STATS_PATH` / `VIEWS_PATH`. The BFF needed no change (generic proxy).
- i18n: `stats.*` in `es`, `en` and `fr` (English and French still need a human review); the settings card text is Spanish with a `// TODO: i18n`, like its neighbours.
- Tests: client, store (reducer, selectors, effects, service), panel, `isUuid` and the view counting of the partner page. Full suite: 516 tests.
- Stacked on the locations/search branch (`feature/locations-and-city-search`, PR #89): merge it first. Depends on directory-backend PR #116 (`/views` and `/stats`).

### Locations (sedes) and search by city, category and text
- Added the **locations screen** of the partner settings (`/partner/settings/locations`), replacing the empty placeholder: list the locations of the business, add, edit, make one the main location and delete (with a two-step confirmation). City is chosen from the cities catalogue; address is required; name, postal code and phone are optional. Errors of the backend (e.g. 403 when the user is not the owner) are shown without closing the form.
- Added the **business search page** (`/search`): filters by city, category and text, paginated, with the filters kept in the URL (`city_id`, `category_id`, `q`, `page`) so a search can be shared, reloaded and reached with the back button. The header search now opens `/search?q=`; `app-search` gained an `initialValue` input.
- Added `CityClient`, `LocationClient` and `BusinessSearchClient` (they unwrap the BFF envelope `{headers, data}`), the NgRx stores `businessSearch` and `locations` (state, actions, reducer, effects, selectors, store service) and the models in `location.model.ts` / `bff-response.model.ts`. New `DFC.RelativePath` entries: `CITIES_PATH`, `LOCATIONS_PATH`, `SEARCH_PATH`.
- The BFF needed **no change**: the generic proxy already maps `/drb/api/v1/general/*` to `/directory-backend/api/v1/*` for every method.
- SSR: the search and the loading of locations run in the browser only (`// SSR: browser-only`); the server renders the page without results.
- i18n: new keys `business_search.*` and `locations.*` in `es`, `en` and `fr`. `fr.json` was empty (invalid JSON); it now holds these keys only. The English and French texts still need human review.
- Tests: specs for the three clients, both stores, the search page, the locations screen, the header and `Search`. Full suite: 487 tests.
- Depends on directory-backend `feature/locations-and-city-search` (cities, locations and `/businesses/search` endpoints): merge that PR first.

- Added initial files for the web project
- Included SSL certificate for the web project
- Created router and proxy for the web project
- Enabled Vault integration for the web project
- Included authentication app client for the backend services
